{"school":{"dbn":"23K518","name":"Kappa V","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"23","district_label":"District 23","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":98,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"985 ROCKAWAY AVENUE, BROOKLYN, NY 11212","phone":"929-305-3576","website":null,"directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/63515","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"KAPPA V recognizes that each child is an individual; all children are creative and possess the ability to succeed. At KAPPA V, we believe that all students are individuals who are capable of learning so our scholars develop social, academic and intellectual habits that inspire them to become tomorrow\u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u0099s leaders. KAPPA V is a college and career ready school that provides rigorous instruction and exposure to opportunities for both our scholars and families to college/university life. This is possible through our interactive curriculum, college tours, and workshops for students and families. Our school has made significant gains on the state exams last year. We are current at 47% in ELA, a 22% increase from the previous year. We continue to push literacy at the forefront of our academics because we know if our students can read and comprehend, they are able to master any subject area. Last year our Math scores increased by 6%. In providing a competitive edge for our students, eighth grade students have the opportunity to earn high school credits by taking Algebra I and Living Environment regents. Additionally, all our scholars have two electronic devices, one to work at home and one to work at school. Our social emotional learning curriculum supported by our teachers and counselors helps our scholars navigate the intricacies of middle school life. Our goal is to build strong scholars, families and community ties throughout our students\u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u0099 middle school experiences while attending to their daily social and emotional needs. Our scholars are engaging in project-based learning, which includes hands-on learning and science projects, the hallmark of our STEM program.  OPUS Dance Theatre, Broadway Junior and the Matisse Foundation are some of the partnerships we have that allow students to explore their artistic side. In these programs, students get the opportunity to engage in dance, photography, steel pan, marching band, majorettes, choir, chess and drama. In our Broadway Jr annual show, students have the opportunity to expressive their acting talents and be part of the stage crew by controlling the lights, sound, moving scenery and curtains. Other enrichment includes Drone Photography, Flight Aviation, Computer Science for All initiative exposes our students to many careers in the field of computer science. Our scholars use these skills to engage in robotics, games/program design and more. Our extended day program runs from Monday through Friday and ends at 6:00pm. Students receive academic intervention, soccer, basketball, track and field, trips, and various arts form and STEM programs. Throughout the year our scholars attends Broadway shows, museums, theme parks and other academic and fun trips to broaden their worldview.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":"3 to Rockaway Av; L to New Lots Av","bus":"B15, B35, B60, B8","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Brownsville","latitude":40.655772,"longitude":-73.906689,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.999],"st":["ok"],"n":[47.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.908,0.93,0.917,0.909,0.911,0.918,0.871],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[197.0,189.0,136.0,112.0,108.0,119.0,130.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,1.0,0.85]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y"